WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.917
Concatenation is different from merging.

00:00:02.917 --> 00:00:06.762
A merge combines columns using a shared key.

00:00:06.762 --> 00:00:11.477
Concatenation usually stacks similar tables on top of each other.

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:17.272
The example contains a January table and a February table with the same structure.

00:00:17.272 --> 00:00:23.552
Pandas concatenates the rows into one larger orders table and resets the index.

00:00:23.552 --> 00:00:31.567
This pattern is common when data arrives in separate monthly, regional, departmental, or batch files.

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:37.002
Before concatenating, check that the column names and meanings are compatible.

00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:42.762
A column called amount should represent the same concept in every file being stacked.
